---
/**
 * Analytics and performance telemetry.
 *
 * STACK CHOICE, stated: Vercel Analytics + Speed Insights. The
 * alternatives were Cloudflare Web Analytics (free, but this site now
 * deploys to Vercel), Plausible or Fathom (nicer dashboards, ~$9/mo),
 * or self-hosted Umami (free, but a database and a service to keep
 * alive for a portfolio's traffic).
 *
 * Picked Vercel's because the hosting already pays for it, it needs no
 * cookies and therefore no consent banner, and Speed Insights reports
 * real Core Web Vitals from real visitors rather than a lab score.
 *
 * What it costs: ~1KB gzipped, and it is Vercel-specific. The beacon
 * posts to /_vercel/insights, so on any other host these load and
 * quietly do nothing. Moving back to Cloudflare means swapping both
 * for the Cloudflare Web Analytics snippet.
 */
---

{/*
  The guard is INSIDE the script, not around it: Astro only bundles a
  top-level <script>, so wrapping this in a template conditional would
  stop it being processed at all.

  import.meta.env.PROD is a build-time constant, so in dev the whole
  branch is dead code and Vite drops it along with the dynamic imports.
  Local page loads never reach the beacon, which matters because the
  point of measuring is that the measurement is trustworthy.
*/}
<script>
  if (import.meta.env.PROD) {
    Promise.all([
      import("@vercel/analytics"),
      import("@vercel/speed-insights"),
    ])
      .then(([analytics, speed]) => {
        analytics.inject();
        speed.injectSpeedInsights();
      })
      .catch(() => {
        /* Blocked by a content blocker, or not on Vercel. Neither is
           a problem the visitor should ever see. */
      });
  }
</script>
